WEBVTT

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:01.910
HITAGI SENJYOGAHARA
SEN JYO GAHARA
NO GROUP

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:03.870
Hello, Senjyogahara?

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.410
What's wrong?

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.790
Does the fact that
you're calling me like this

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:10.080
mean that this round of trouble
has already been resolved?

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.710
I'm not quite done yet.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.460
I'm sorry, I couldn't resist.
I was feeling a bit helpless.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.840
I see. Well, leave everything
concerning Hanekawa to me.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.470
Did something happen to Hanekawa?

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.850
You haven't heard from Kanbaru?

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:28.600
Heard what?

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.060
Well, if you haven't heard...

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.980
You can hear the story directly from her
once you come back.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.690
You know, Senjyogahara...

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.490
There's one thing I want you to tell me.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:47.410
One year ago, when Kanbaru entered
Naoetsu High School and came to visit you...

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.740
Honestly speaking, how did you feel?

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:55.000
Let's see. Frankly, it felt like a burden...
her feelings, that is.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.670
But that was partly a showing
of how light-hearted I was

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:02.130
with my inability to tolerate
the weight of her burden.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.010
If I were to be together with Kanbaru,

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:09.760
I'd probably have to become someone
that could bear that weight.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.350
Even now, that's how I feel
as I try to improve myself.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:16.020
It may not look it, but...

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.020
I'm making quite the effort
to become Araragi's bride.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:21.530
HITAGI SENJYOGAHARA
SEN JYO GAHARA
NO GROUP

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:24.030
No, it's not necessarily that...

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.080
This may be our last call,

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.920
so can I ask you something
that you might upset you?

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.170
HITAGI SENJYOGAHARA
SEN JYO GAHARA
NO GROUP

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.920
If someone with better qualifications
were to confess his love to you, what would you do?

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.300
In that case,
I think I'd switch to the new guy 100%.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.310
You're amazing...
You're amazing because you can actually say that.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:57.600
I know there's no bond that's absolute.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:01.570
I learned that from watching my parents.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.190
Senjyogahara... No, that's—

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.570
An absolute bond, when you think about it,
is pretty scary.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:13.450
That's why you need to work hard,
so you don't get dumped for someone else.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:18.210
Even if you can't become a special person in general,
you can be a special person for someone.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.460
A special person for someone...

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:21.840
HITAGI SENJYOGAHARA
SEN JYO GAHARA
NO GROUP

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:27.720
<i>I make endless efforts to be
a special person for Kanbaru and Araragi.</i>

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:33.180
Rest assured, Araragi,
you're already plenty special enough of a person.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.980
For myself, for Kanbaru - for Shinobu, too.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.980
<i>We are all choosing you.</i>

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.980
You really understood what I meant...
That's amazing.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:45.320
HITAGI SENJYOGAHARA
SEN JYO GAHARA
NO GROUP

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:50.370
<i>I am your girlfriend after all.
I was very happy that you called me.</i>

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:52.080
I love you.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:53.620
I love you.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:59.370
When I get back, a little more...
we should have conversations like this more often.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:02:59.670
HITAGI SENJYOGAHARA
SEN JYO GAHARA
NO GROUP

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:02.000
<i>Yes. I'll be waiting in my birthday suit.</i>

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.920
Kanbaru's perverseness
is strongly affected by you, isn't it?

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.220
OWARIMONOGATARI

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:12.970
SHINOBU MAIL, PART SIX

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:28.490
Then, let's hurry up and start this,
so we can hurry up and end it.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:29.740
Come here.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.620
Okay. All good now.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:43.630
We're done getting ready.
Now you're prepared for battle.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.630
Done getting ready?
Done getting ready with just that?

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.260
Come now, hold on a moment...

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.470
What happened to the pairing, Sir Araragi?

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:58.390
You aren't going to stay that weak
and duel against me like that... Are you?

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.520
THAT VOICE, IT WAS NO LONGER
THAT WHICH HE HAD PILFERED FROM ME.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.390
IT HAD CHANGED INTO THAT OF HIS OWN.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:09.400
Oh, brother. It looks like the bond between you
and Kiss-shot wasn't as weak as I had feared.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:14.910
I can't believe that she'd send her servant
into combat in such a weak state.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:20.120
<i>I don't want to win
because of Shinobu's power.</i>

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.170
<i>I want to win,
and be an supporting power to Shinobu.</i>

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:25.250
Well, fine...

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:27.880
But Lady Izuko.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:33.340
If this is the case, I'd like you to select
a method of dueling that has a handicap.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.180
I wouldn't like to hear unpleasant excuses.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.600
Of course.

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:42.440
I plan on using an unchanging format of dueling
that has been used since ancient days.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:46.190
As occasion permits, it should allow you two
to compete in a fair manner.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:58.410
Call it an imaginary demon sword
"Kokoro Watari" or something.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:00.830
Of course, electricity is running through it.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:05.580
Well, yeah, just think of it as a stun gun
that works for both of you.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:10.670
First off, I'll have you two stand back to back,
on either side of this wooden sword.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:16.260
And, on my count,
walk forward ten steps from there.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:19.140
The tenth step will be the last,
as the battle will begin there.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.480
The one who dashes to this wooden sword
and deals a blow to his opponent is the winner.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.730
Of course, you can take the wooden sword
from your opponent and then deliver a blow.

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:30.610
Strictly speaking, the criteria
for this match is a "one-blow duel."

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:32.740
In other words...

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:36.030
More than just making the conditions fair,

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:41.120
this is you looking out for Sir Araragi,
so he doesn't die in this duel.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.620
Impressive that you came up
with something like this.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.500
Any other questions?

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:46.370
Negative.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.380
Araragi, do you have any questions?

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:51.090
I'm an amateur in terms of
both swordsmanship and combat...

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:55.630
So can I at least be lectured from a specialist
concerning that ten-step run?

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.140
A specialist?

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:03.930
Okay. A handicap of that level
should be all right to add.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.730
Since it's 7:30 right now...

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:09.650
The duel will begin at 8 o'clock sharp.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:13.650
Both of you, be diligent in your warm-ups.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:21.080
Guessing from your height, Araragi-senpai,
your stride is 72 centimeters wide.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:24.910
In other words, a span of ten steps
would be 7 meters and 20 centimeters.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.670
A marathon has a strategy
just for marathons,

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:30.920
and the 100-meter dash has a strategy
just for the 100-meter dash.

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:35.220
Likewise, to run seven meters,
there's a strategy to run seven meters.

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:38.680
However, the task here may be
how to reserve some strength for later.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:40.300
Why a task?

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:44.100
I mean, running the dash isn't the end of it all.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:47.690
You have to grab the wooden sword
and deliver a blow with it, right?

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:49.310
Oh, right.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:53.230
I think that in the end,

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:56.570
the swordplay after pulling out the wooden sword
will be more important.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:58.780
Araragi-senpai,
even if you draw the wooden sword,

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:01.530
if he dodges your attack,
takes the wooden sword

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:05.580
and pummels you with it,
all of the effort will be for nothing.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.120
That's true...

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.830
But all I can say about that is,
"Whatever will be, will be."

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.210
I can't trouble you that much, after all.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:16.630
Then, at the least, I'll lend you my shoes.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.340
We wear the same size, right?

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:20.470
Yeah, thanks.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:26.730
What is this?

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:31.520
Wh-What in the world has been happening
in the short time I haven't been at school?

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:33.690
Kanbaru, do you know anything about this?

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:36.740
No, I have no clue at all,

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:39.740
but all I can think of is that after
Hanekawa-senpai's home was burned down,

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:43.990
Senjyogahara-senpai informed Karen and Tsukihi
of the situation to get their help

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:47.370
by letting her stay at Araragi-senpai's house.
That's the only thing I can think of.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.370
That's probably the right answer!

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:50.370
Wait, a fire?

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.750
Her home was burned down?

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:53.750
What's that story about?

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.130
My oh my. Her story also seems to be
reaching its climax...

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:58.630
What will you do, Koyomin?

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.430
Izuko, you know something about this?

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:02.470
Hanekawa is...

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:05.430
No, wait, do you even know
who Hanekawa is?

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:08.220
And what's this about
what I'm going to do? Do what?

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.020
I know everything.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.270
I mean, it's the tiger, Koyomin.

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:16.400
The tiger that ironically saved you
back in the cram school ruins...

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:21.780
Tsubasa has apparently decided to face-off against
that big tiger that controls the flames of purgatory.

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:26.790
Actually, Tsubasa isn't the only one in a crisis.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.500
Your girlfriend Senjyogahara
is also in a crisis.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:30.250
What?

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:35.880
Perhaps, as we stand here now,
they may be burning furiously...

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:40.340
If you're going to save her, you need to go
as soon as possible - right now if you can.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:43.340
You should, by abandoning meaningless this duel.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:49.270
It saves me a lot more
if you don't fight this duel.

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:51.690
I'd be troubled if you were to die.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:54.100
I can't be the one that breaks the rules,

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:57.900
so if you could break the rules of your own accord,
that would help me a whole bunch.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:01.860
Koyomin, good for you.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.820
You have the perfect reason
to cancel the duel.

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.830
You need to choose, Koyomin.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:14.460
Are you going to stay here, so you can fight
a duel that accomplishes nothing,

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:18.130
or start running in order to save
Tsubasa and Senjyogahara?

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:19.880
Are you going to choose Shinobu?

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:21.510
Are you going to choose Tsubasa?

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.630
Are you going to choose Senjyogahara?

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:27.640
Of the three of them...
Who do you love the most?

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.350
Kanbaru. I'm counting on you.

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:30.270
You can count on me.

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:32.850
I just have to go to your house, right?

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:36.440
Yeah. Tell Karen to let you in.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.360
I'll catch up soon enough,
so I want you to check things out first.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:40.730
Details understood!

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:47.280
Are you sane? This is unthinkable.

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:50.540
Can you really only see
what's directly in front of your eyes?

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:56.370
It's true that by letting Suruga Kanbaru,
who's a lot more mobile than you, run for you,

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.880
you might be able
to deal with both situations.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.010
Tsubasa just might be able to face the perils
with only her own powers.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:05.930
You're the only one who can fight here,

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:08.760
so it may be the correct answer
for you to remain.

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.260
However, that's all logic.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:13.270
Humans have emotions.

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:17.400
Didn't she send you that text
because she believed in you?

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:20.400
Are you going to betray that trust?

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:27.660
With this betrayal,
maybe they'll never trust you again?

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:31.660
That may be so.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:37.040
But, I have faith in them.

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:40.500
I believe in Hanekawa, and in Senjyogahara.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.170
From the bottom of my heart.

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:42.920
IF IT'S ABOUT THOSE TWO, WHO ARE SPECIAL TO ME.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:43.800
IF IT'S TSUBASA HANEKAWA

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:44.550
AND HITAGI SENJYOGAHARA.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:48.890
A guy by the name of Koyomi Araragi
sometimes prioritizes a young girl,

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:51.640
more than the one
he owes his life to, or his lover.

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:53.640
I have faith they'll understand that.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:11:02.570
I'd someday like to believe in people
like I was lending my cellphone out to someone.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.120
Totally makes me laugh.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:22.340
As the master, she's making preparations
for the battle between her slaves, huh?

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:25.090
No, in this case, it's the prize, isn't it?

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:28.760
Like, whoever wins is given
the demon sword or something.

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:34.470
Perhaps. In any case, the wooden sword
I took the effort to prepare is split in two,

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.140
so we'll have to use the real thing.

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:46.280
Koyomin, first one. We're a little past time now,
but let's have you begin.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:50.780
As planned, stand with your backs to one another,
with the sword between you.

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:59.290
Coming so close, but yet,
why is my master Kiss-shot not showing herself?

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:04.790
Does Kiss-shot not want
to meet me that much?

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:07.260
Sir Araragi, what do you think?

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:13.350
Is the dispute between you and me
nothing but deeply troubling for Kiss-shot?

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:18.810
For you, Sir Araragi,
what meaning is there to this duel?

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:23.060
The meaning for me is something
not even you'll understand.

00:12:26.150 --> 00:12:29.860
You may be a special person,
a chosen one.

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:33.870
I may not be special nor chosen.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:39.410
Nobody might be able to take your place,
and anyone might be able to take my place.

00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:41.290
But still...

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.210
You can't be me.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:51.550
There are a lot of people that can take my place,
but I'm the only me.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:56.430
You're not me, and I'm not you.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.060
Isn't that how it is?

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:02.560
One.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:04.310
Two.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:06.060
Three.

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:07.770
Four.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:09.530
Five.

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:11.320
Six.

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:13.030
Seven.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:14.700
Eight.

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:16.320
Nine.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:17.530
Ten!

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.960
Meme's... Oh, so that's how it is.

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:13.380
Surprising... This is really beyond my expectations.

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:17.010
To think that the rule I set as whoever
delivers one blow (hito-tachi) is the winner

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:20.470
would be twisted around so whoever
delivers one touch (hito-tacchi) is the winner!

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:33.230
K-K-iss-shot, Kiss-shot, Kiss-sho—

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:59.760
Kiss-shot... kiss... shot...

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:04.770
Kiss-shot... Kiss-shot!

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:11.230
Well, I don't know
what age I'll live to be...

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:14.070
But if we see each other again
while I'm alive...

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:16.320
<i>If we meet again...</i>

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:18.450
<i>....we'll meet again.</i>

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:31.580
You don't have to apologize. I forgave you.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:45.020
I'm the one that was at fault...

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:51.860
Seishiro...

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.870
I was glad to see you.

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:06.540
Because I thought I'd never see you again.

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:10.870
But I won't be seeing you anymore.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:18.970
Currently, I have someone
that's more important to me than you.

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:22.890
For a little while longer,
I'd like to be someone who's there for him.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:30.390
<i>It wasn't refreshing. It didn't feel good.</i>

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:31.020
NAOETSU HIGH

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:33.900
<i>By being clearly told,
it actually made it harder to feel at ease instead.</i>

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:35.940
<i>There was no distinct salvation.</i>

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:41.150
<i>But, even then,
400 years after he committed it...</i>

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:47.410
<i>...his suicide had finally succeeded.</i>

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:55.420
Yes, yes. And so, what happened
after that, Araragi-senpai?

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.750
What you'd call an epilogue...
Or the punchline for this episode.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:01.010
Everything after that is exactly like
what I've said before.

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:04.840
I met up with Kanbaru,
who had gone to my house ahead of me,

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:05.050
REFERENCE BOOK

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:07.640
and joined up for the part
about Hanekawa's tiger.

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:12.810
I headed to where Hanekawa was,
and Kanbaru headed to where Senjyogahara was.

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:16.150
I see, I see.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:19.190
Well, thank you very much, Araragi-senpai.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:22.490
With this, all the puzzle pieces
have fallen into place.

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:27.990
There were places where the outline of the story
slightly contradicts the stories I've heard thus far.

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:32.620
But as the listener of all kinds of stories,
making sense of such contradictions

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:35.830
is what I, Ougi Oshino, have fun doing.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:37.090
KOYOMIST

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:44.680
<i>Today is March 13th... early morning
of the day of my actual college entrance exams.</i>

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:47.180
Then, I'll be going home for today.

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.180
If you're still alive, I'll see you again.

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:50.640
One more thing.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:55.520
Did Shinobu, in the end,
finish eating the entirety of her first minion?

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:58.360
Well... I said so, didn't I?

00:17:58.360 --> 00:17:59.730
Without missing anything?

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.530
Yeah, without missing anything.

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:02.860
Even the suit of armor?

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.530
She ate it... I think.

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:10.660
Perhaps she did, but...

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:15.080
Is that an important point?

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:19.590
I mean, that suit of armor is the blood and flesh
of the first apparition killer,

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:20.920
as well as its skeleton, right?

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:26.180
Then, if you melted that
suit of armor down, and then forged it...

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:30.930
You could make an additional one, you know...
another demon sword "Kokoro Watari."

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:34.810
Not only that, but if things go well,
even the short sword "Yume Watari" as well.

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:36.310
<i>"Yume Watari"?</i>

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:42.440
If I was Gaen, I'd retrieve the armor
before Shinobu ate it.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:46.910
Surprisingly enough, maybe that's why
she summoned Episode there.

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:50.240
There's no reason for Gaen
to do such a thing.

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:54.200
I think Shinobu simply ate the armor as well.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.370
Yeah, I think that's how things went.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:00.710
Then, lastly, allow me
to give a thank-you gift

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:03.210
by answering one more question
you have, Araragi-senpai.

00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:06.760
A question I have?
What is this question I have?

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:08.510
Seishiro Shishirui.

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:09.890
SEISHIRO SHISHIRUI

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:12.890
That's the full name
of the first apparition killer.

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:18.230
Even you, Araragi-senpai, like to be fully aware of
the name of your romantic rival, correct?

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:27.610
I just happened to hear
what you were talking about.

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:28.490
<i>This again?</i>

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:29.240
IT'S ALL RIGHT.
I AVOIDED CONTACT WITH THAT GIRL.

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:29.990
WHEN SHE WAS PASSING BY,
I CLUNG TO THE CEILING TO AVOID HER.

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:33.450
Devil boy, you really are so chatty
around that girl.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:34.910
Don't you think you babble too much?

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:38.210
You think so?
I don't think that's the case.

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:41.130
If you're fine with it, devil boy,
then that's fine.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:45.010
I'm going to head to North Shirahebi Shrine now.
You want to come with me?

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:47.260
Where is that?

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:51.510
Don't forget it.
You forget way too much.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:54.470
It's the place where your master went missing.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.140
I'm not going on a morning date
with you, devil boy.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:20:00.770
Though, that said, there is something
I want you to tell me as well.

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:01.650
What is that?

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:04.650
Devil boy, are you happy
that you've become a vampire?

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:09.400
The first apparition killer
was saying something along the lines

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:14.740
of "what benefits I'll see"
from devil boy being with Shinobu-sensei.

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:21.080
In the end, devil boy, you were unable
to present the merits of such a situation to him.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:23.290
But the feeling behind it still hasn't changed?

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:29.920
Devil boy, do you still feel that by you being together
with Shinobu-sensei, nobody becomes happy?

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:34.180
I still feel that way.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:39.180
Nobody becomes happy,
and nobody can become happy.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:43.520
By me being a vampire,
by me being together with Shinobu,

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:45.440
I can only cause trouble to others.

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:48.940
More than anyone else,
I'm bringing misfortune to Shinobu.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.950
Though, that can come across
as just an excuse.

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:57.240
"Please pardon me,
because I won't be happy.

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:01.120
Please forgive me,
because I won't try to become happy.

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:03.580
Please gloss over me."
That's what it might sound like.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:05.590
Or, it might sound like you're asserting.

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:10.800
"Since we're so misfortunate,
don't blame us. Aren't we pitiful?"

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:15.720
Hey, devil boy, can it be that you think of putting up
with misfortune or unfortunate circumstances

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:17.970
as putting forth a good effort?

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:22.810
In society, things like that
are called "doing nothing."

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:25.400
Don't think you'll be forgiven
because you're misfortunate.

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:27.070
You should be aiming
for the happy ending.

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:29.320
Or do you want me to stomp
on your face again?

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:33.450
Ononoki, you're really strict.

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:39.240
Staying misfortunate is negligence,
and not trying to become happy is cowardice.

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:43.080
If you stay like that, the forefather that
committed suicide can never be truly rewarded.

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:44.960
I'll make note of that.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:52.090
<i>Nobody has become happy.
Not I, not Shinobu, no one.</i>

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:53.090
FOR NOW, THAT'S WHAT I THINK—

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:54.090
THAT'S WHAT I STILL THINK.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:22:02.480
<i>But perhaps, a long time from now,
far, far in the future - say, like 400 years from now,</i>

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:07.110
<i>that train of thought may be slightly altered,
I think among other things...</i>

00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:10.320
<i>...it's fine. Even if we aren't happy,</i>

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:13.740
<i>fortunately for us,
we still have plenty of time ahead of us.</i>

00:22:14.150 --> 00:22:19.240
<i>Time alone - time to think, time to live -
is there to the point we're disgusted.</i>

00:22:19.490 --> 00:22:22.620
<i>We have so much time that
a corpse can rot and turn to ash.</i>

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:27.380
<i>But such time being taken from us...</i>

00:22:27.960 --> 00:24:20.169
<i>...perhaps was also a matter of time as well.</i>
